Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ak820pro: the RTC's PCF write and host corrections, for
 the wireless clock (codex's design review, 10-20; drafted by Gremlin for the
 Mac session's review) -- must-fix 1, an accepted host correction restarts the
 legacy trim's window, and the discipline waits out a slew; must-fix 2,
 host_sync_gen moves only on an accepted correction, never on a RETRY or a
 REJECT (raw HID's replies unchanged); must-fix 4, PCF requests carry
 generations, so a write planned for an older request cannot consume a newer
 one; must-fix 5, the PCF is stale from an accepted correction until a write
 of its generation lands: no snap, acquisition or wake calendar from it
 meanwhile (a wake keeps the board's calendar and adds the PCF's elapsed
 seconds), and a given-up write is not pending (a dead PCF never holds the
 board awake) but is asked for again a minute on; should-fix 8, the
 phase-correct write waits for a slew to finish. The bookkeeping is
 rtc_pcf_sync.h, pure, with scripts/rtc_pcf_sync_test.c; health page 4 [24]
 reports stale

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Mm219BiSCsx6uwtXcZ7a9G
